# Moatmat Teacher - Project Structure Rules

## Overview
This is a Flutter application for teachers using Clean Architecture with BLoC pattern. The app name is "moatmat_teacher" and it's an educational platform for teachers to manage students, tests, banks, and various educational resources.

## Architecture Pattern
The project follows **Clean Architecture** with clear separation of concerns:
- **Domain Layer**: Business logic, entities, use cases, repository interfaces
- **Data Layer**: Data sources, models, repository implementations  
- **Presentation Layer**: UI, state management (BLoC/Cubit), widgets



### `/lib/Core` - Shared Infrastructure
- **`/injection`** - Dependency injection setup (GetIt)
- **`/services`** - Core services (Supabase, cache, encryption, etc.)
- **`/resources`** - App resources (colors, fonts, spacing, images, etc.)
- **`/widgets`** - Reusable UI components
- **`/functions`** - Utility functions (dialogs, PDF, Excel, math, parsers)
- **`/validators`** - Input validation logic
- **`/errors`** - Error handling (exceptions, failures)
- **`/constant`** - App constants (classes, governorates, materials)
- **`/app`** - App-level configuration

### `/lib/Features` - Business Features (Clean Architecture)
Each feature follows the same structure:
```
/feature_name/
  /domain/
    /entities/     - Business entities
    /repository/   - Repository interfaces
    /use_cases/    - Business use cases
  /data/
    /data_source/  - Remote/local data sources
    /models/       - Data transfer objects
    /repository/   - Repository implementations
```



### `/lib/Presentation` - UI Layer
Each presentation module contains:
- **`/state`** - BLoC/Cubit state management
- **`/views`** - Screen/page widgets
- **`/widgets`** - Feature-specific widgets

**UI Modules:**
- `auth` - Login, registration, account management
- `home` - Dashboard/home screens
- `students` - Student management UI
- `tests` - Test creation/management UI
- `banks` - Question bank UI
- `groups` - Group management UI
- `attendance` - Attendance tracking UI
- `reports` - Reports and analytics UI
- `notifications` - Notifications UI
- `scanner` - Camera/scanning UI
- `picker` - Item selection UI
- `folders` - File/folder management
- `questions` - Question creation/editing
- `equations` - Math equation editor
- `export` - Data export functionality
- `videos` - Video management
- `statistics` - Analytics dashboard
- `purchases` - Payment UI
- `tests_results` - Test results display
- `banks_results` - Bank results display
- `outer_tests_results` - External test results

## Platform-Specific Code

### `/android` - Android Configuration
- `app/build.gradle.kts` - Android build configuration
- `app/google-services.json` - Firebase Android config
- `app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml` - Android manifest

### `/ios` - iOS Configuration  
- `Runner/Info.plist` - iOS app configuration
- `Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist` - Firebase iOS config
- `Podfile` - iOS dependencies

### `/web` - Web Configuration
- `index.html` - Web entry point
- `manifest.json` - PWA manifest






## Development Guidelines

### File Naming Conventions
- Use snake_case for file names
- Use descriptive names that indicate purpose
- Suffix files with their type: `_cubit.dart`, `_bloc.dart`, `_widget.dart`

### Code Organization
- Follow Clean Architecture layers strictly
- Keep business logic in domain layer
- UI logic only in presentation layer
- Use dependency injection for all services

### Feature Development
1. Start with domain layer (entities, use cases, repository interface)
2. Implement data layer (models, data sources, repository)
3. Create presentation layer (BLoC/Cubit, views, widgets)
4. Add proper error handling and validation

### Testing
- Unit tests in `/test` directory
- Follow same structure as `/lib` for test organization

## Special Notes
- App supports Arabic localization
- Uses custom Tajawal font family
- Implements Firebase for backend services
- Supabase for real-time features
- Math equation rendering capabilities
- QR code scanning functionality
- PDF generation and export features
- Video player integration
- Camera integration for scanning
